the tale of viking warrior omleth's  revenge in the northmen has plenty of  twists and turns leading up to an epic  vengeance-filled climax the ending is  full of startling revelations but what  does it all mean to omelet's destiny  stay tuned because this is the ending of  the northmen explained  in the northmen audiences first meet  omleth as a young boy who idolizes his  father king alvin deal as well as the  kingdom he expects to inherit that of  course doesn't go according to plan  avondale's brother fuelner executes a  brutal plan that ends with the king's  death filner's brutal takeover of alvin  deal's kingdom sends young omleth into  exile and he does not emerge again until  years later now a man and a member of a  fearsome viking tribe for nearly the  entirety of the northmen omelette is  guided by three goals to avenge his  father save his mother gudrun and kill  fjornier to earn his vengeance  as an adult omleth stops at nothing to  achieve these goals as he murders his  way through filner's village in iceland  even when it grows clear that he may die  in the process the character embraces  the prospect of death from injury on the  battlefield as a personal victory that  will send him to valhalla or as it's  called in the film vol whole omleth runs  the risk of truly losing himself in the  process of achieving a goal he set for  himself as a child solely in the name of  revenge at one point omelette sets aside  a necklace given to him by his father so  he can disguise himself as a slave to  get closer to fjallnir and in that  moment he ceases to be himself instead  he becomes a tool of prophetic revenge  omelette's meetings with the cirrus and  other visions tell him that his children  with olga will rule the kingdom that  should have been omelets in the future  for almost his destiny lies on the  battlefield with his uncle shortly after  omlet's destiny has revealed him and he  remembers his vengeful oath the viking  warrior learns that his uncle has fled  to iceland this flight happens because  after deposing alvin deal fionnier is  defeated by another ruler fleeing to the  small north atlantic island to start a  new life after an arduous journey omleth  finally arrives in iceland to exact his  revenge but the northman offers a messy  conclusion that sets it apart from other  vengeance sagas omleth doesn't really  have a kingdom to return to and to take  for his own once he's defeated his uncle  all that's left of fjallner's domain is  a small farming community to infiltrate  fjolner's village omleth brands himself  and travels as a slave across the ocean  once under the control of his uncle the  prince sees that fjolnier's home is just  a small village in iceland filner lives  there with gudrun and their son gunnar  filner's older son torrer and a small  grouping of villagers and their slaves  filner has already been humbled by  external forces by the time omlith  reaches him and aside from murdering  alvin deal he seems to be a capable  leader in fact when we meet him again  he's teaching gunar the importance of  doing physical labor alongside the rest  of the village it's a moment reminiscent  of young amla's experience with his  father when fjolnier and omelette  finally do battle in head-to-head combat  at the base of an active volcano known  as the gates of hell omelette finally  achieves his goal of killing his  traitorous uncle however considering the  state filner is already in by the time  omelette reaches him it's hard to say  how satisfying reaching this conclusion  of his journey actually is  robert eggers portrays amleth as a  single-minded protagonist he's driven  solely by his need to achieve vengeance  for his father's death and the film  rarely suggests that omelets will fail  at that goal your fake is sick and you  cannot escape it  as an adult the exiled prince is a  violent and fearsome combatant he even  kills a man larger than himself when he  is conscripted to play an early version  of the irish sport hurling when omelet  is captured by fjornier toward the end  of the second act of the film his  captivity is brief ravens release him  from his bonds suggesting his revenge  isn't just his goal but a true destiny  bestowed on him by the gods and  completing the gods mission omelette  ascends to valhalla signified by the  electrifying visions of a valkyrie  flying through the night sky omelette's  revenge plays out even as he learns that  the reality of his family's existence  was not what he once thought the film's  first act implies that fjomir keeps  gudrune against her will after alvin  diehl's death but in a surprise twist we  eventually learned that it was gudrun  herself who plotted to kill alvin deal  brought into his kingdom as a slave  khadrun was forced into marriage when  alvin deal took notice of her this  startling revelation makes one third of  omelet's vengeful mantra obsolete it  further emphasizes the ways in which the  northmen muddies the waters of a classic  revenge saga not only is amleth driven  by a single-minded drive to fulfill his  destiny but when he learns the truth he  realizes that he doesn't even have a  clear idea of who he is actually seeking  revenge on ultimately his own violent  destruction is the only way his story  can end  the northmen is the third outing from  robert eggers following two films that  won him immense critical acclaim while  the witch and the lighthouse were both  made on relatively modest budgets the  northmen and its roughly 90 million  dollar price tag represents a huge leap  forward for the filmmaker with the film  receiving its own glowing reviews from  critics does this mean we can expect  more big big-budget blockbusters in  egger's signature style in the future in  the lead-up to the film's release eggers  has been candid in interviews about the  difficulties he faced in making the  northmen despite the significant amount  of action in the movie eggers noted to  the new yorker that neither he nor  cinematographer jaren blaschke had never  shot a significant action scene before  the project furthermore eggers admitted  that his filming methods left little  extra footage to make any changes to the  film something he ended up doing after a  series of test screenings eggers opened  up to the guardian about modifying the  film after submitting it for test  screenings a process he had not  undergone on his first two films while  he clarified that the give and take with  the studio helped produce the most  entertaining version of the movie he  could make he also alluded to not  necessarily enjoying the process while  it sounds like eggers is happy with the  end result of the northmen he has also  said that he doesn't want to step away  from making smaller scale films he noted  that he has had meetings with larger  studios but that he doesn't feel his  skills as a filmmaker are useful for  franchise blockbuster filmmaking so we  may see another grand epic from eggers  down the line but don't expect to see  him helming a marvel cinematic universe  film anytime soon check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite movies  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

